From: Andrew Sim <andrewsimz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: cap the RX refill page_pool on 256 MiB boards

The RX refill page_pool is created with pool_size equal to the refill
ring's entry count. Its recycle ring keeps up to that many order-1 pages
beyond the ones posted to the hardware, which with 1024 entries is up to
8 MiB per radio that no meminfo field reports. On a 256 MiB IPQ6000
board MemAvailable was seen falling steadily with both radios up while
Slab and AnonPages stayed flat.

With ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M, cap pool_size at 256 pages. Pages returned
when the recycle ring is full go back to the page allocator.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Sim <andrewsimz@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -876,6 +876,16 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* The page_pool recycle cache holds up to pool_size pages beyond those
+ * posted to the ring. With order-1 pages and a 1024-entry refill ring that
+ * is 8 MiB per radio a 256 MiB board cannot spare, so cap it there.
+ */
+#ifdef CPTCFG_ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M
+#define DP_RX_PP_POOL_SIZE(n)	min_t(u32, (n), 256)
+#else
+#define DP_RX_PP_POOL_SIZE(n)	(n)
+#endif
+
 static int ath11k_dp_rxdma_ring_buf_setup(struct ath11k *ar,
 					  struct dp_rxdma_ring *rx_ring,
 					  u32 ringtype)
@@ -893,7 +903,7 @@
 		struct page_pool_params pp_params = {
 			.order = DP_RX_PP_ORDER,
 			.flags = PP_FLAG_DMA_MAP,
-			.pool_size = num_entries,
+			.pool_size = DP_RX_PP_POOL_SIZE(num_entries),
 			.nid = NUMA_NO_NODE,
 			.dev = ar->ab->dev,
 			.dma_dir = DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL,
